        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0782" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2330</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of Commerce</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sweet</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 11</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is enclosed herewith for your
                    information and such comment as you may care to make a copy of a circular signed
                    by the British Vice Consul. This circular sets forth that an arrangement has
                    been made whereby American shippers may inform themselves in advance whether
                    their consignments will be regarded as unobjectionable under the British
                    military regulations, or whether any of the circumstances would require
                    investigation, and to this end an office has been established provisionally at
                    the British Embassy, Washington, D. C, which will give to intending shippers in
                    satisfactory cases letters of assurance to facilitate the passage of shipments
                    through the British naval patrol.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. F. Sweet</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d604-a1.xml" xpointer="d604-a1"/>
